1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,484
The staff week had to become evidence, and evidence is a demanding master.

2
00:00:04,484 --> 00:00:11,617
Among the three hundred pages of notes, only a handful could survive a stranger's reading.

3
00:00:11,617 --> 00:00:16,521
“It is easy to be nice about a school,” the teacher said.

4
00:00:16,521 --> 00:00:19,286
“It is harder to be accurate.

5
00:00:19,286 --> 00:00:31,213
Please treat the week as a problem, not as a story.” Much of the material, she added, was already stale the day it was written.

6
00:00:31,213 --> 00:00:34,987
The team already knew where the weakness was.

7
00:00:34,987 --> 00:00:41,566
A pretty table can hide a hasty sample; a cheerful summary can bury a misery.

8
00:00:41,566 --> 00:00:46,495
“We must observe, not celebrate,” Lin wrote.

9
00:00:46,495 --> 00:00:51,064
“You are crazy,” Maya said, laughing.

10
00:00:51,064 --> 00:01:09,589
“But you are also right.” The bulk of the evidence was delicate: a girl who had never been asked, a kid who had learned to read from a cereal box, and a boy who could remember every word of a notice but not the name of the office that posted it.

11
00:01:09,589 --> 00:01:13,438
The eventual report was a surgical document.

12
00:01:13,438 --> 00:01:19,967
It listed what the group had seen, what it had assumed, and where the two differed.

13
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:27,425
A skilled typist prepared three copies; a handsome folder carried them to the faculty office.

14
00:01:27,425 --> 00:01:30,789
An early draft had been much longer.

15
00:01:30,789 --> 00:01:42,167
One sentence, quoted later in the student paper, read: “The honor of a school is not in its buildings but in the questions it allows.”

16
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:45,426
The irony was not lost on them.

17
00:01:45,426 --> 00:01:54,009
A university that charged high tuition could not discriminate between students who asked and students who stayed absent.

18
00:01:54,009 --> 00:02:07,531
An enterprising professor, eager to help, wanted a mightier conclusion than the data allowed, and the uneasy silence that followed was, in turn, an education.

19
00:02:07,531 --> 00:02:11,400
A clever remark about statistics broke it.

20
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:15,424
“You ask for the impossible,” she said.

21
00:02:15,424 --> 00:02:18,218
“No,” Maya said.

22
00:02:18,218 --> 00:02:26,442
“We ask for the eventual.” The wit in the room was merry; the impatience was not.

23
00:02:26,442 --> 00:02:37,854
A cloudy afternoon brought a fantastic offer: a conference slot, a congratulatory letter, and a chance to present the week as a triumph.

24
00:02:37,854 --> 00:02:47,611
Those pages, however, would need a badly lit corridor to look impressive, and the team refused the triumphant part.

25
00:02:47,611 --> 00:02:59,354
A commonplace sentence, they decided, was worth more than a pretty one, and an ironic footnote about the information they lacked could heighten the contrast.

26
00:02:59,354 --> 00:03:06,817
The work was tricky, the timetable adventurous, and one table already obsolete.

27
00:03:06,817 --> 00:03:11,161
Their proficiency would be measured by what they left out.

28
00:03:11,161 --> 00:03:14,470
“Yes,” the professor said.

29
00:03:14,470 --> 00:03:18,028
“That is the art of it.”
